+## Parent runtime observation
+
+`observe_current_nvidia_runtime(cuda_driver_version,
+expected_cuda_runtime_library_path)` is the explicit parent-only discovery seam
+used before creating a `CompileRequest`. It requires an already current regular
+CUDA context, queries the complete live device identity/resource set through
+PyPTO's private Driver boundary, and returns an immutable
+`NvidiaRuntimeObservation` containing `NvidiaTargetInfo`, numeric Driver and
+Runtime API versions, the canonical Runtime-provider path, and diagnostic
+context address/ID values.
+
+The release-form `cuda_driver_version` string is caller-supplied provenance;
+the numeric Driver API version is queried independently. The CUDA Runtime must
+already have been loaded globally by the parent framework. PyPTO resolves only
+`cudaRuntimeGetVersion` from the existing process symbol table, uses `dladdr`
+to require that its canonical provider equals the caller-audited expected
+library, and fails if either check is absent; it never opens a `libcudart`
+soname. The caller remains responsible for establishing why that expected file
+belongs to the selected framework environment. Observation loads no Cubin,
+retains no context or stream handle, and does not replace the independent live
+checks performed by executable prewarm and launch. A fork child must use
+spawn/exec before observation; the PID latch covers PyPTO's private Driver use,
+not arbitrary CUDA initialization by other libraries.
 
 ## Prewarm and loader compatibility
 
